@tradition rec-film-night
// W3 (rec writer; lead 18: fields from plans/rec-traditions-plan.html FINAL and the brief; RA owns the format).
// Film night in the auditorium: Saturdays 20:00-22:15, from the first Saturday after the first Captain's all-hands (lead
// 17's call 1: when ship-wide events exist). It waits on the flag rec.film.moved (RA sets it, and stops the hand-written
// junior common room film night then; the JCR becomes a quiet Saturday hangout). The screen comes down, the house lights
// go down, popcorn from the galley. A gathering.
k: 496
title: Film night
when: weekly saturday
at: 20:00-22:15
min: 45
jitter: 30
where: 7 room Auditorium: rec:seat
hold: none
who: juniors 50%, everyone 35%
anim: everyone talk
from: The rec deck
flag: rec.film.moved

== mail
- Film night tomorrow, {time} in the auditorium. The screen comes down, the lights go down, and there's popcorn from the galley.

== ask
- Film tonight. I'm sitting at the back. I always fall asleep in the good bit.   #funny
- Are you coming to film night? Bring a cushion, or come early for the good seats.

== here
- Shh, it's starting.
- Pass the popcorn. Please. Thank you.

== thanks
- You find a seat as the lights go down. The film starts with a long shot of a lighthouse. Somebody sighs happily.   #warm

== chatter
- What's on at film night? Nobody ever knows till it starts.
- I cried at the film. It was the lighthouse. It's always the lighthouse.   #funny
